# Image Annotation Extension

**Status:** implemented

**Trigger syntax:**
```
<!--After the image block either ![]() or <img> tag -->
^(x, y): Annotation content
```

**Description:**
Adds annotation to image by having two arguments, positions from left and top in pixels.
This means read image data first before putting the annotations on top of the image.
The annotation is a dashed-line circle, raised and show text tooltip on hover.

**Input example:**
```
<!--After the image block either ![]() or <img> tag -->
^(400, 300): Image annotation description
^(800, 800): Example of bottom-right annotation

Text content
^(100, 100): This is ignored and shown as plain content text
```

**Expected output:**
```html
<figure class="img-annotated"><img src="https://example.com/pic.png" alt="alt text"><span class="img-note" tabindex="0" style="left:400px;top:300px" aria-label="Image annotation description"><span class="img-tip">Image annotation description</span></span><span class="img-note" tabindex="0" style="left:800px;top:800px" aria-label="Example of bottom-right annotation"><span class="img-tip">Example of bottom-right annotation</span></span></figure>
<p>Text content
^(100, 100): This is ignored and shown as plain content text</p>
```
The parser emits px coords relative to the image's natural (original) size.
Generator-side behavior: `main.js` converts px → % of `naturalWidth/Height` once
the image loads (notes track image bounds at any rendered width), centers bubbles
on the coord (22px desktop / 28px touch), and positions the `.img-tip` tooltip
within screen bounds on hover/focus — clamped to side margins, flipped below the
bubble when near the viewport top. Default CSS placement (above-center) is the
no-JS fallback.

**Edge cases / notes:**
- Image must be read from parser step.
- Only whole-line markdown images (`![alt](src)`) carry annotations. Raw `<img>`
  tag lines do NOT — the parser runs with `html: false`, so source-driven raw
  attributes stay escaped (XSS-safe default). Supporting `<img>` would need an
  attribute whitelist.
- Annotation lines attach to the image line directly above them (no blank line
  between). Blank lines or non-matching lines detach the annotation → rendered
  as plain text.
- Coordinates must be non-negative integers; non-numeric/negative coords keep
  the line as plain text.
- Annotation text is HTML-escaped (quotes included).
- Tooltip is a real `.img-tip` element (not a CSS pseudo-element) so JS can
  measure and clamp it within screen bounds; without JS it renders above-center
  and may clip at the edge.
- `ponytail:` px coords are relative to the image's natural size and converted
  to % by `main.js` at runtime (browser knows natural size natively — no
  build-time image fetching). If JS is disabled, notes render at natural-size
  px positions and drift on scaled images — acceptable progressive fallback.
